/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Seeds and saves are copied or symlinked into tests/fixtures/ by hand: they are
# large and not ours to redistribute. See crates/pahoa-pickle/tests/fixtures.rs.
#
# Ignore those artifacts specifically rather than the whole directory, so that
# small generated fixtures we *do* want committed — golden vectors, recorded
# reference outputs from the differential harness — can live alongside them.
**/tests/fixtures/*.archipelago
**/tests/fixtures/*.apsave
**/tests/fixtures/*.zip

# ...with one deliberate exception. The poisoned multidata is an attack sample
# rather than somebody's seed: 38 KB, no personal data, and the actual file that
# crashed a host in the wild. `MultiData::parse` has no encoder beside it, so a
# malicious seed cannot be written back out and holding the real one is the only
# way to test that it stays refused. See crates/pahoa-multidata/tests/poison.rs.
!**/tests/fixtures/poisoned_multidata.archipelago

# Python bytecode from the development-time scripts in tools/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
